    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a2">

                <pb facs="0574" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg474"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 139.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Notice to emigrants and emigration agents.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Metropolitan Police Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Great
                                Scotland Yard</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">14th day of Oct.</hi>,
                            1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Whereas there is reason to believe that a system of solicitation extensively
                    prevails to induce persons to emigrate from Great Britain to the United States
                    for the purpose of joining the Mormon community at Salt Lake, in the Territory
                    of Utah, this notice is to warn all persons that the law of the United States
                    prohibits the practice of polygamy existing in the Mormon community, and renders
                    any person who engages therein liable to heavy fine and a long period of
                    imprisonment.</p>
                <closer><signed>E. Y. HENDERSON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner of
                            Police of the Metropolis, acting under the immediate authority of Her
                            Majesty’s Principal Secretary of State for the Home
                        Department.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
